      "text": "Dr. Khalifa: Well, we need to comment on the first, on the title of the Sura. You know, a believer appreciates God differently from people who are unaware, or who are not strong believers. You can see here that the title of the Sura is the Winds. And we learn from the first few verses that the winds, their main job is to carry clouds and bring bounties. We need that water. So, in order to appreciate God and these simple words, just imagine yourself sending ten astronauts to space. You, sending ten astronauts to space, and you tell them \"okay, you're gonna be out there for three years, and when you need water, I made an invention in the spaceship, so there'll be these clouds on top of you, and they will give you water.\" You're sending them into space. And you devise that system that will give them water, clean water. When they pollute the water they have on the spaceship, it's gonna, you know, one of... number one purification processes is distillation. So, when they pollute, their own water is gonna evaporate, it's gonna be pure water, and come down again. So, you tell them that to assure them that they will have enough water supply for three years, or five years, ten years, or whatever. You're sending them. Just imagine that. See, God sent this spaceship with five billion astronauts. You and me, we are astronauts. That's right. And God gave us this system. God devised this system, where the water evaporates and then comes down by... the winds drive the clouds here. How far are we from the ocean? We're far from the ocean. But these clouds came to us from the ocean, by the wind. It's a traveling system. And it sends down pure water. You appreciate God if you think, if you imagine sending ten astronauts in space and you tell them \"I'm going to give you the exact percentage of oxygen for you to breathe.\" Now in 1967, we were technologically advanced people. 1967. But we put three astronauts in a capsule in an atmosphere of 100% oxygen. Pure oxygen, r